From d50a1b4c3c5380b97b934ed882c98a707e09c180 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 21:55:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(oneshot): pin RoCE proxy thread to dedicated fast core
 within cpuset

Upstream base: christopherowen/dgx-spark-networking 1fd6a1fbd8dc4884057046d1ebd93d585c9e4bcf (tree 8cc28a5cd3e683c1f114ed843453e3ce34f323e0).

Rationale:
On GB10 heterogeneous ARMv9 nodes (10x Cortex-A725 efficiency cores at 2.808 GHz / capacity 718..731 vs. 10x Cortex-X925 performance cores at 3.9 GHz / capacity 997..1024), resolve_proxy_cpus previously read only cpu_capacity across all host cores without intersecting sched_getaffinity, selected all 10 fast cores as a shared pool under SPARKNET_ROCE_PROXY_CPU=big, left the proxy thread unpinned when SPARKNET_ROCE_PROXY_CPU was unset, and did not lower timer slack for idle nanosleep wakeups.
1. Discover fast performance cores via cpufreq/cpuinfo_max_freq with fallback to cpu_capacity, and intersect candidate CPUs with sched_getaffinity(0) so container cpusets and taskset masks are respected.
2. Add fast/auto/dedicated single-core selection (selecting the highest-numbered fast core in sched_getaffinity, CPU 19 on GB10) and comma-separated CPU list/range parsing alongside big and none.
3. Set prctl(PR_SET_TIMERSLACK, 1UL) on sparknet-proxy so idle nanosleep wakeups do not incur 50 us default timer slack.
4. Default SPARKNET_ROCE_PROXY_CPU to fast in SparknetOneShotAllReduce when unset in the environment.

Quality implications:
Bit-identical collective reductions and wire ABI 10; affects only host proxy thread CPU affinity and wakeup timer slack.

Tests:
- python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v (97 passed, including ASan/UBSan C proxy simulator with fast/auto/dedicated, range, and sched_getaffinity intersection assertions).

Upstream status: local candidate patch for dgx-spark-networking.
